0	section	Talking to the Guildmaster after talking to Oziach
1	line	Guildmaster	Greetings!
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	What is this place?
1	option	I talked to Oziach...
2	line	Player	I talked to Oziach and he gave me a quest.
2	line	Guildmaster	Oh? What did he tell you to do?
2	line	Player	Defeat the dragon of Crandor.
2	line	Guildmaster	The dragon of Crandor?
2	line	Player	Um, yes...
2	line	Guildmaster	Goodness, he hasn't given you an easy job, has he?
2	line	Player	What's so special about this dragon?
2	line	Guildmaster	Thirty years ago, Crandor was a thriving community with a great tradition of mages and adventurers. Many Crandorians even earned the right to be part of the Champions' Guild!
2	line	Guildmaster	One of their adventurers went too far, however. He descended into the volcano in the centre of Crandor and woke the dragon Elvarg.
2	line	Guildmaster	He must have fought valiantly against the dragon because they say that, to this day, she has a scar down her side,
2	line	Guildmaster	but the dragon still won the fight. She emerged and laid waste to the whole of Crandor with her fire breath!
2	line	Guildmaster	Some refugees managed to escape in fishing boats. They landed on the coast, north of Rimmington, and set up camp but the dragon followed them and burned the camp to the ground.
2	line	Guildmaster	Out of all the people of Crandor there were only three survivors: a trio of wizards who used magic to escape. Their names were Thalzar, Lozar and Melzar.
2	line	Guildmaster	If you're serious about taking on Elvarg, first you'll need to get to Crandor, and to my knowledge, the only way to do that is by sea.
2	line	Player	So I just sail over there? Seems easy enough.
2	line	Guildmaster	If only that were true. The island is surrounded by dangerous underwater reefs. You'll need a map to guide you through them and a ship capable of doing so.
2	line	Guildmaster	And then of course there's the dragon herself. Once you reach Crandor, you'll need some kind of protection against her breath.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Where can I find a map to Crandor?
3	line	Player	Where can I find a map to Crandor?
3	line	Guildmaster	After what happened, people were afraid of enraging the dragon. Most maps to the island were destroyed, but I have heard that one survived. It was held by Melzar, Thalzar and Lozar.
3	line	Guildmaster	However, the three apparently split the map into three pieces, which each of them taking one piece.
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	Where is Melzar's map piece?
4	line	Player	Where is Melzar's map piece?
4	line	Guildmaster	Melzar built a castle on the site of the Crandorian refugee camp, north of Rimmington. He's locked himself in there and no one's seen him for years.
4	line	Guildmaster	The inside of his castle is like a maze, and is populated by undead monsters. Maybe, if you could get all the way through the maze, you could find his piece of the map.
4	line	Guildmaster	Adventurers sometimes go in there to prove themselves, so I can give you this key to Melzar's Maze.
4	box	The Guildmaster hands you a key.
4	action	other
3	option	Where is Thalzar's map piece?
4	line	Player	Where is Thalzar's map piece?
4	line	Guildmaster	Thalzar was the most paranoid of the three wizards. He hid his map piece and took the secret of its location to his grave.
4	line	Guildmaster	I don't think you'd be able to find out where it is by ordinary means. You'll need to talk to the Oracle on Ice Mountain.
4	action	other
3	option	Where is Lozar's map piece?
4	line	Player	Where is Lozar's map piece?
4	line	Guildmaster	A few weeks ago, I'd have told you to speak to Lozar herself, in her house across the river from Lumbridge.
4	line	Guildmaster	Unfortunately, goblin raiders killed her and stole everything. One of the goblins from the Goblin Village probably has the map piece now.
4	action	other
2	option	What kind of ship do I need?
3	line	Player	What kind of ship do I need?
3	line	Guildmaster	Quite a specific one I'm afraid. Even with a map, very few ships will be able to navigate the reefs around the island. You're going to need one of Crandorian design.
3	line	Guildmaster	If there's still one in existence, it's probably in Port Sarim. However, a ship will also need a captain, and I'm not sure where you'd find one willing to sail to Crandor!
3	cond	If the player has completed Pandemonium:
4	line	Player	Could I not just captain it myself? I have some experience in that area.
4	line	Guildmaster	I suppose you could, but given you have a dragon to be dealing with, I'd suggest getting someone else to worry about the captaining for you.
3	action	other
2	option	How can I protect myself from the dragon's breath?
3	line	Player	How can I protect myself from the dragon's breath?
3	line	Guildmaster	That part shouldn't be too difficult, actually. I believe the Duke of Lumbridge has a special shield in his armoury that is enchanted against dragon's breath.
3	action	other
2	option	What's so special about this dragon?
3	action	above
2	option	Okay, I'll get going!
3	line	Player	Okay, I'll get going!
3	action	end
