0	section	Talking to the Oracle
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	I seek a piece of the map to the island of Crandor.
2	line	Player	I seek a piece of the map to the island of Crandor.
2	line	Oracle	The map's behind a door below, but entering is rather tough. This is what you need to know: You must use the following stuff.
2	line	Oracle	First, a drink used by a mage. Next, some worm string, changed to sheet. Then, a small crustacean cage. Last, a bowl that's not seen heat.
2	action	end
1	option	Can you impart your wise knowledge to me, O Oracle?
0	section	Using respective items on the door
0	section	Searching the chest
1	box	As you open the chest, you notice an inscription on the lid:
1	box	Here I rest the map to my beloved home. To whoever finds it, I beg of you, let it be. I was honour-bound not to destroy the map piece, but I have used all my magical skill to keep it from being recovered.
1	box	This map leads to the lair of the beast that destroyed my home, devoured my family, and burned to a cinder all that I love. But revenge would not benefit me now, and to disturb this beast is to risk bringing its wrath down upon another land.
1	box	I cannot stop you from taking this map piece now, but think on this: if you can slay the Dragon of Crandor, you are a greater hero than my land ever produced. There is no shame in backing out now.
1	box	You find a map piece in the chest.
1	action	end
