0	section	Talking to Klarense
1	line	Klarense	Hello there! Interested in buying this fine ship? I'm sure I can offer her to you for a much better price than any of those shipwrights ask for!
1	line	Player	A much better price? What's the catch?
1	line	Klarense	Well, she's not quite seaworthy right now...
1	line	Player	Not seaworthy? Why would I want to buy her then?
1	line	Klarense	Because this isn't just any ship! This is the Lady Lumbridge, one of the last Crandorian ships! Despite her size, she's one of the most agile shipShould be "ships" around!
1	line	Player	Except she's not seaworthy...
1	line	Klarense	No, but a bit of work will quickly sort that out!
1	option	I'd like to buy her.
2	line	Player	I'd like to buy her.
2	line	Klarense	Of course! I'm sure the work needed to do on it wouldn't be too expensive.
2	line	Klarense	How does 2,000 gold sound? I'll even throw in my cabin boy, Jenkins, for free! He'll swab the decks and splice the mainsails for you!
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Yep, sounds good.
3	cond	If the player does not have enough coins:
4	line	Player	Yep, sounds good.
4	line	Player	...except I don't have that kind of money on me...
4	action	end
3	cond	If the player has enough coins:
4	line	Player	Yep, sounds good.
4	line	Klarense	Okey-dokey! She's all yours!
4	action	end
2	option	I'm not paying that much for a broken boat!
3	line	Player	I'm not paying that much for a broken boat!
3	line	Klarense	That's fair enough, I suppose.
3	action	end
1	option	Why is she damaged?
2	line	Player	Why is she damaged?
2	line	Klarense	Oh, there was no particular accident, just years of wear and tear. It's been a long time since Crandor was destroyed and she's had several owners since then. Unfortunately, not all of them looked after her.
2	action	other
1	option	I think I'll pass.
2	line	Player	I think I'll pass.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Klarense after purchasing the Lady Lumbridge
1	line	Klarense	Hello, captain! Here to inspect your new ship? Just a little work and she'll be seaworthy again.
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	So, what needs fixing on the ship?
2	cond	If the player has not fixed the ship:
3	line	Player	So, what needs fixing on this ship?
3	line	Klarense	Well, the big gaping hole in the hold is the problem. You'll need a few wooden planks hammered in with steel nails to fix it.
3	action	other
2	cond	If the player has fixed the ship:
3	line	Klarense	I dunno. It looks fine to me.
3	line	Player	But you said it needed fix-
3	line	Klarense	Yes, but that was before you fixed it!
3	action	other
1	option	Would you sail this ship to Crandor for me?
2	line	Player	So would you like to sail this ship to Crandor for me?
2	line	Klarense	Crandor? You're joking, right?
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Yes. Ha ha ha!
3	line	Player	Yes. Ha ha ha!
3	line	Klarense	Crandor's not something we sailors joke about. You can't sail from here to Catherby, or Entrana, or Ardougne without going past that accursed island.
3	line	Klarense	You can't get close to it because of the reefs, but you can always see it.
3	line	Klarense	Sometimes you can see a dark shape in the sky, circling the island. That's when you have to sail on as quick as you can and pray it's not hungry. Every year, more ships are lost to that dragon.
3	action	other
2	option	No. I want to go to Crandor.
3	line	Player	No. I want to go to Crandor.
3	line	Klarense	Then you must be crazy.
3	line	Klarense	That island is surrounded by reefs that would rip this ship to shreds. Even if you found a map, you'd need an experienced captain to stand a chance of getting through
3	line	Klarense	and, even if I could get to it, there's no way I'm going any closer to that dragon than I have to. They say it can destroy whole ships with one bite.
3	action	other
1	option	What are you going to do now you don't have a ship?
2	line	Player	What are you going to do now you don't have a ship?
2	line	Klarense	Oh, I'll be fine. I've got work as Port Sarim's first lifeguard!
2	action	other
1	option	Can I board the ship now?
2	line	Player	Can I board the ship now?
2	line	Klarense	Sure thing, she's all yours.
2	action	end
