1	option	Can you sail this ship to Crandor?
2	line	Player	Can you sail this ship to Crandor?
2	line	Cabin Boy Jenkins	Not me, sir! I'm just an 'umble cabin boy. You'll need a proper cap'n.
2	line	Player	Where can I find a captain?
2	line	Cabin Boy Jenkins	The cap'ns round 'ere seem to be a mite scared of Crandor. I ask 'em why and they just say it was afore my time,
2	line	Cabin Boy Jenkins	but there is one cap'n I reckon might 'elp. I 'eard there's a retired 'un who lives in Draynor Village who's so desperate to sail again 'e'd take any job.
2	line	Cabin Boy Jenkins	I can't remember 'is name, but 'e lives in Draynor Village an' makes rope.
2	action	end
0	section	Interacting with the sawmill operator after buying the Lady Lumbridge
1	line	Sawmill operator	Hello there. Are you in need of planks or construction supplies?
1	line	Player	As it so happens, I do need some wooden planks!
1	line	Sawmill operator	Fortunately for you, you've come to the right place!
1	line	Sawmill operator	Less fortunately for you, I'm on a legally mandated break right now.
1	line	Player	Could you make an exception? I need the planks to go and fight a dragon.
1	line	Sawmill operator	A dragon? How are planks going to help you with that?
1	line	Player	I'm repairing a boat to sail to Crandor so that I can slay Elvarg.
1	line	Sawmill operator	Crandor? Elvarg? Well, far be it from me to stop you trying.
1	line	Player	So you'll make some planks for me?
1	line	Sawmill operator	I will, but I can't make you too many. It'll be just my luck if King Roald decides to audit this place and I've been making planks off the clock.
1	line	Player	What do you need from me to make some planks?
1	cond	If the sawmill operator has already made 9 planks:
2	line	Sawmill operator	Unfortunately I can't make any more planks for you without drawing attention to myself. You're going to have to source them elsewhere.
2	action	end
1	line	Sawmill operator	You'll have to provide the logs and 100 coins for each plank. Just basic logs will do for what you need.
1	line	Sawmill operator	As a reminder, I can't make you very many without risking an audit, so I'll have to stop at nine planks.
1	cond	If the player doesn't have any normal logs or coins:
2	line	Sawmill operator	You'll need to bring me some more logs.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player has logs but not enough coins:
2	line	Sawmill operator	Those planks cost 100 coins. You don't have enough money for all of them.
2	action	end
0	section	Reparing the Lady Lumbridge
1	cond	If the player does not have any planks:
