0	section	Ned
1	line	Ned	Why, hello there, [lad/lass/kid]. Me friends call me Ned. I was a man of the sea, but it's past me now. Could I be making or selling you some rope?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	You're a sailor? Could you take me to Crandor?
2	line	Player	You're a sailor? Could you take me to the island of Crandor?
2	line	Ned	Well, I was a sailor. I've not been able to get work at sea these days, though. They say I'm too old.
2	line	Ned	Sorry, where was it you said you wanted to go?
2	line	Player	To the island of Crandor.
2	line	Ned	Crandor?
2	line	Ned	But... It would be a chance to sail a ship once more. I'd sail anywhere if it was a chance to sail again.
2	line	Ned	Then again, no captain in his right mind would sail to that island...
2	line	Ned	Ah, you only live once! I'll do it!
2	line	Ned	So, where's your ship?
2	cond	If the player hasn't bought the ship yet:
3	line	Player	Well, I don't actually have a ship yet.
3	line	Ned	Ah, well. Let me know when you do. The place to look would be Port Sarim.
3	action	end
2	line	Player	It's the Lady Lumbridge, in Port Sarim.
2	line	Ned	That old pile of junk? Last I heard, she wasn't seaworthy.
2	line	Player	I fixed her up!
2	line	Ned	You did? Excellent!
2	line	Ned	Just show me the map and we can get ready to go!
3	cond	If the player has the completed map:
4	line	Player	Here you go.
4	box	You hand the map to Ned.
4	line	Ned	Excellent! I'll meet you at the ship, then.
4	action	end
3	cond	If the player has all three map parts:
4	line	Player	Here you go.
4	box	You hand the map parts to Ned.
4	line	Ned	Excellent! I'll meet you at the ship, then.
4	action	end
3	cond	If the player does not have the completed map:
4	line	Player	Uh...yeah...about that. I don't actually have a map on me.
4	line	Ned	You'd better go find it, then. I'm not going to go sailing off without a map to show me where to head!
4	action	end
1	option	Yes, I would like some rope.
1	option	No thanks, Ned. I don't need any.
