1	option	Can you sail this ship to Crandor?
2	line	Player	Can you sail this ship to Crandor?
2	line	Cabin Boy Jenkins	Not me, sir! I'm just an 'umble cabin boy. You'll need a proper cap'n.
2	line	Player	Where can I find a captain?
2	line	Cabin Boy Jenkins	The cap'ns round 'ere seem to be a mite scared of Crandor. I ask 'em why and they just say it was afore my time,
2	line	Cabin Boy Jenkins	but there is one cap'n I reckon might 'elp. I 'eard there's a retired 'un who lives in Draynor Village who's so desperate to sail again 'e'd take any job.
2	line	Cabin Boy Jenkins	I can't remember 'is name, but 'e lives in Draynor Village an' makes rope.
2	action	end
0	section	Protection from a dragon's breath
0	section	Talking to Duke Horacio
1	line	Duke Horacio	Greetings. Welcome to my castle.
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	I seek a shield that will protect me from dragonbreath.
2	line	Player	I seek a shield that will protect me from dragonbreath.
2	line	Duke Horacio	A knight going on a dragon quest, hmm? What dragon do you intend to slay?
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Elvarg, the dragon of Crandor island!
3	line	Player	Elvarg, the dragon of Crandor island!
3	line	Duke Horacio	Elvarg? Are you sure?
3	select	Well, are you sure?
3	option	Yes
4	line	Player	Yes!
4	line	Duke Horacio	Well, you're a braver man than I!
4	line	Player	Why is everyone so scared of this dragon?
4	line	Duke Horacio	Back in my father's day, Crandor was an important city-state. Politically, it was as important as Falador or Varrock and its ships traded with every port.
4	line	Duke Horacio	But, one day when I was little, all contact was lost. The trading ships and the diplomatic envoys just stopped coming.
4	line	Duke Horacio	I remember my father being very scared. He posted lookouts on the roof to warn if the dragon was approaching. All the city rulers were worried that Elvarg would devastate the whole continent.
4	select	Select an Option
4	option	I'd better leave that dragon alone.
5	line	Player	I'd better leave that dragon alone.
5	line	Duke Horacio	That's a relief. I would hate to see such a promising adventurer cut down in [his/her/their] prime.
5	action	end
4	option	So, are you going to give me the shield or not?
5	line	Player	So, are you going to give me the shield or not?
5	line	Duke Horacio	If you really think you're up to it then perhaps you are the one who can kill this dragon.
5	box	The Duke hands you a heavy orange shield.
5	line	Duke Horacio	Take care out there. If you kill it...
5	line	Duke Horacio	If you kill it, for Saradomin's sake make sure it's really dead!
5	action	end
3	option	No
4	line	Player	No.
4	line	Duke Horacio	Very wise. There are some monsters that are best left alone.
4	action	end
2	option	Oh, no dragon in particular
3	line	Player	Oh, no dragon in particular. I just feel like killing a dragon.
3	line	Duke Horacio	I don't have an infinite supply of these shields, you know. I'll only give one for a truly worthy cause.
3	action	end
1	option	Have you any quests for me?
1	option	Where can I find money?
