0	section	Sailing to Crandor
1	line	Captain Ned	Ah, it's good to feel the salt spray on my face once again!
1	line	Captain Ned	And this is a mighty fine ship. She don't look much, but she handles like a dream.
1	line	Player	How much longer until we reach Crandor?
1	line	Captain Ned	Not long now! According to the chart, we'd be able to see Crandor if it wasn't for those clouds on the horizon.
1	box	Clouds surround the ship.
1	line	Cabin Boy Jenkins	Looks like there's a storm coming up, cap'n. Soon we won't be able to see anything!
1	line	Captain Ned	Oh, well. The weather had been so good up until now.
1	line	Player	Did you see that?
1	line	Captain Ned	See what?
1	line	Player	I thought I saw something up above us.
1	line	Captain Ned	It's the dragon!
1	line	Captain Ned	We're going to sink!
1	line	Player	Look! Land ahead!
1	line	Captain Ned	We're going to crash!
1	box	You are knocked unconscious and later awake on an ash-strewn beach.
0	section	Talking to Ned after reaching Crandor
1	line	Captain Ned	Now I see why all the other captains said I'd be mad to go near Crandor. It looks like we're stranded.
2	line	Player	Don't worry about that. I found a secret passage in the dragon's lair that leads off the island!
2	line	Captain Ned	Oh, that's good. I'll be able to get back to Draynor somehow,
2	line	Captain Ned	if I can sneak past all the skeletons and demons on this island!
2	action	end
1	action	end
